WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:08.740
For me, I think data is life. Everyday
we're using data, but I, as a data

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:14.320
scientist, I'm using data to quantify
human behavior around the world.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:20.540
So our research as a whole seeks to
understand whether we can use online

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:26.900
data to better understand human behavior
and our experience in the world we live in.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:34.860
My inspiration for the tracking
process cities dates back to 2013 during

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:40.770
the time of the major protests around the
world. So I analyzed twenty-five million

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:46.530
images taken and uploaded to a picture
sharing platform on social media across

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:51.809
two hundred and forty-four countries and
continents. Analyzing almost twenty-five

00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:57.120
million images could have taken me ten
months to run it on my own machine, but

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.250
using Azure I was able to run it in less
than a week. I'm no longer afraid to add

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:09.240
more data in my analysis. I feel braver
about my research to explore more data

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:15.990
and scale up my project. I'm aiming to
highlight the potential value of online

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:21.450
data, especially online images, as a new
source of global and cheaply available

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:26.060
measures of human behavior around the
world.

